---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<Legal
  title="Privacy policy"
  description={`How ${site.name} collects, uses and stores your personal information.`}
>
  <p>
    This page explains what {site.legal.entityName} does with the personal information you give us
    through this website. It is written to describe what actually happens, not to cover every
    imaginable case.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    {site.legal.entityName}, running yoga studios in Anjar and Adipur, Kutch, Gujarat, India. Our
    registered address and phone number are at the bottom of every page of this website.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect, and why</h2>
  <p>The only personal information this website collects is what you send through the contact form:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name and mobile number, so we can reply.</li>
    <li>Your email address, studio preference, what you are interested in, and your message, if you fill them in.</li>
    <li>
      The internet address (IP address) your message came from. This is used only to stop one person
      or machine flooding the form, and for nothing else.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We use these details only to answer your message. Visitors do not have accounts, and there is no
    advertising, no tracking across other websites, and no analytics on this site.
  </p>

  <h2>Where it is kept, and who else can see it</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell your information and we do not share it for marketing. It reaches these companies
    only because they run parts of this website for us:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Supabase</strong> stores the messages sent through the contact form. Our data is held in Mumbai, India.</li>
    <li><strong>Resend</strong> emails the studio a copy of each message, when that is switched on.</li>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> serves this website and keeps short-lived server logs.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google</strong> receives your IP address when your browser loads the fonts and the
      embedded maps on this site. This happens on almost every website and we do not control it.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We will also hand over information if the law requires it, for example a valid order from a court
    or the police.
  </p>

  <h2>What is stored in your browser</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing. This website sets no cookies of its own and stores nothing on your device. The embedded
    Google Maps are run by Google, which may set its own.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Messages from the contact form: until we have dealt with them, and then for up to a year in case
    you come back.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights, and asking us to delete your message</h2>
  <p>
    Under India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, you can ask us to show you what we hold
    about you, correct anything wrong, or delete it. Write to{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>, or message us on{' '}
    <a href={`https://wa.me/${site.whatsapp}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">WhatsApp</a>, with the
    name and number you used, and we will reply within thirty days.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are not happy with our answer, you may complain to the Data Protection Board of India.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    If you are under eighteen, please ask a parent or guardian to send the message for you.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the date at the top of this page changes with it.
  </p>
</Legal>
